<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imru' al-Qais</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imru' al-Qais was a pre-Islamic Arab poet, a prince of the royal house of Kinda, often regarded as the greatest poet of the Jahiliyya. His ode is one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muallaqat">Mu'allaqat</a>, the most famous collection of early Arabic poetry. After his father was killed he spent years trying to avenge him and recover the Kindite kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imru-al-qais.jpg" alt="Imru' al-Qais" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imru_al-Qays.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
